course: dictionary
lesson: 14807
title: Purification: making things clean and pure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Purification is a noun, so it names a process. It comes from the verb purify, which means to make something clean and pure. The ending -ation turns the verb into a noun for the action, so purification means the act of making something pure.
explain: «The new plant uses purification to make the river water safe to drink.» The word water shows what is being cleaned, and the word plant shows that this is a process. Purification means taking out dirt and harmful things so that the water becomes safe.
explain: Purification can also mean a spiritual clean. «Before the prayer, the people took part in a purification ceremony.» The clues are prayer and ceremony: this is about making a person or place spiritually clean, not about soap and water. Always check the words around the word to see which meaning fits.
fact: Purification is a noun, so it can name a process or a ceremony.
fact: «Purification» means making something clean and pure by removing dirt or harmful things.
fact: Water purification can use filtering, boiling or chlorine to make water safe to drink.
fact: In science, purification means separating a pure substance from a mixture.
fact: In church, the Feast of the Purification, also called Candlemas, is on 2 February.
exercise: «The water purification plant made the river water safe to drink.» What does purification mean here? | Making water warm for a bath | *Making water clean and safe | Making the river loud | Making the river deeper
exercise: «Mum bought purification tablets for our camping trip.» What are purification tablets used for? | Making your hair shiny | *Cleaning water so it is safe to drink | Making you sleepy at night | Keeping sandwiches fresh
exercise: In science, purification means separating a pure substance from a mixture. Which one is an example? | Making a cake | *Separating pure salt from a salty mixture | Freezing an ice cube | Mixing paint with water
test: «Before the prayer, the family took part in a purification ceremony.» What is a purification ceremony? | A school sports day | A cooking lesson | *A ritual to make people spiritually clean | A sleepover with friends
test: What kind of word is purification? | Adjective | *Noun | Adverb | Verb
exam: Which sentence uses purification correctly? | «The purification ran fast down the hill.» | «Purification is a loud, happy colour.» | «I purification my bike every Sunday.» | *«Water purification makes the river water safe to drink.»
